25,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"Our staffing is critical. The late-turn pool is depleted, and roadway crews are well below establishment, though lift maintenance has capacity.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"Mid-city runs are slower than they used to be, but the crowds clear at the same rate. The real delay is waiting for connections.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"We have a lapsed grant for construction, but the technology and operating budgets have been trimmed. Ticketing fees are eating our paving budget.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Servas,,"History repeats. A late-evening pilot was successful years ago, and most accessibility rebuilds finished on time, though some lane priorities failed.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Working in pre-war shells is a gamble due to unrecorded voids. Also, ferry and rail offices can't even agree on data terms.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, if the technology budget is trimmed, we cannot afford a complex new system that requires heavy staffing.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Jonathan, if the data terms are a mess, any integrated system will be a nightmare to implement.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, you're right. We need to be mindful of the long-term operating costs, not just the initial grant.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Takumi, it is interesting that the delays are in the connections. We should look for a solution that addresses flow.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Servas, the ""flow"" might be blocked by those pre-war voids if we try to dig into the old stations.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Servas, the staffing shortage for late turns makes any extension of hours very risky.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"If the mid-city surface route is slowing down, maybe a dedicated corridor is the answer?","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Takumi, but Benjamin's paving rates are climbing. Rebuilding boarding islands will be expensive.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,Servas,,"We must avoid the mistakes of the past. If lane priorities failed before, we should be cautious with bus corridors.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I agree with Servas. The ground is unpredictable, and the bureaucracy between operators is worse.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
