50,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"The candidates are A: Night Service, B: Bus Corridor, C: Station Access, and D: Fare Platform. I cannot support A due to staffing.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Takumi,,"B addresses the mid-city slowdown, but @Benjamin mentioned the paving costs. I'm torn between B and D.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"D is attractive because it cuts those separate contractor fees I found, though the tech budget is tight.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Servas,,"A has a successful pilot in its history, but C's accessibility records are generally positive.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,C is too risky with the pre-war voids. D is a bureaucratic nightmare given the committee minutes.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Jonathan, if D is a nightmare, then C is the only one that fits the available lift maintenance capacity.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Takumi,,But C doesn't fix the connection delays I found in the audits. B is the most direct fix for the city center.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Takumi, the capital ledger has a construction balance. B uses that, but D saves us money on annual fees.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@Asuka, the staffing for A is a real issue. I think C is the most stable, historically speaking.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"I still distrust the shells in C. B is surface-level, which avoids the voids, even if paving is pricey.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,Asuka,,I'll vote for C. It uses the maintenance capacity we actually have.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Takumi,,I'll go with B. It's the only one that actually addresses the passenger's time.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,I'll vote for D. Reducing the contractor fees is the only logical long-term financial move.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,Servas,,I agree with Asuka. C is a proven path with a high completion rate.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,I'll vote for B. It avoids the underground risks and the inter-operator data wars.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
